Article 4 (Public Disclosure of Evaluation Results, etc.)
(1) The Minister of the Interior and Safety, a Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a special-case city shall, by April 30 of the following fiscal year, disclose on the respective Internet websites of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, the relevant Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, Do, Special Self-Governing Do, or special-case city the main contents of project reports submitted by non-profit, non-governmental organizations under Article 9 (1) of the Act and the results of evaluations conducted under Articles 2 and 3 (hereinafter referred to as "evaluation results, etc."). Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety, a Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a special-case city operates a separate Internet website established to manage support projects for non-profit, non-governmental organizations, the same information shall also be disclosed on that website. <Amended on Jul. 26, 2017; May 1, 2023>
(2) The evaluation results, etc. disclosed under paragraph (1) shall include the following matters: <Amended on Jul. 26, 2017; May 1, 2023>
1. The purpose and contents of public-interest projects carried out by the relevant non-profit, non-governmental organization;
2. Project implementation performance compared with the implementation plan set out in the project plan;
3. Project results under Article 2 (1);
4. Details of project expenditures under subparagraph 3 of Article 11 of the Decree;
5. Evaluation results under Articles 2 and 3;
6. Overall opinions of the Minister of the Interior and Safety, the Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of the special-case city.
